    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "america\nSERVICE STANDARDS\nREVISION DATE 2015.05",
      "How to Use This Document\nA consistent, easy-to-read format allows readers to quickly find and identify different types\nof information.\n1. Subject heading - Introduces a new subject\nExample:\nPlating Entrees\n2. Reminder Table - imparts general information\nExample:\nRemember the following before plating entrees:\n• Wash hands.\n• Start with a clean galley, tidy counter and return service items to carts and carriers if not in use.\n• Maintain easy access to equipment and supplies by folding cart doors open against sides and returning them\nto under counter.\n• Pull out retractable galley tables.\n• Arrange plating guides on counter so that they are easy to see and follow when plating.\n• Leave individual foil pans in the oven until ready to plate.\n• Remove plates and entrée pans from the oven no more than two at a time.\nIntroduction - Page 1\nCh. 4. - General Procedures\nCh. 1 - Brand\nCh. 2 - Guest Service Philosophy\nCh. 3 - Guest Service Standards"
    ],
